From dd72c1ce9d5b1feed00600fbffeb1c7b57440ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:39:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aw87339: let the OUT pin switch take the amplifier out of the
 path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The board describes "Spk0 OUT" and "Spk1 OUT" as pin switches so that
the UCM headphone device can mute the speakers, which are fed by the
codec's headphone stage. They had no effect: the amplifier was a SPK
widget followed by an OUTPUT widget named OUT, and DAPM treats a SPK
widget as an output endpoint of its own, so with the OUT pin disabled
the path through "SPK PA" stayed complete and the amplifier powered up
with every headphone stream. Music played on the headset and the
speakers at once.

Make the SPK widget the endpoint and name it OUT. The pin switch keeps
its name ("Spk0 OUT Switch", the UCM profile is unchanged) and now
disconnects the amplifier itself; the anti-pop ordering of the SPK
widget (power up last, down first) stays.

Disclosure: LLMGD-2 · origin O1 (the model traced the DAPM path and wrote the change; the author tested speaker and headset playback)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A2; flags=T; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=claude-opus-5-5; retrieval=none
---
 sound/soc/codecs/aw87339.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/aw87339.c b/sound/soc/codecs/aw87339.c
index fb23e4c87..2a0b05cef 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/aw87339.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/aw87339.c
@@ -149,14 +149,18 @@ static const struct snd_soc_dapm_widget aw87339_dapm_widgets[] = {
 	 * Anti-pop: as a speaker widget the amplifier is powered up last and down first.
 	 * It switches on once the codec output has settled (POST_PMU) and off before the
 	 * codec powers down (PRE_PMD), so it never amplifies the codec's power transients.
+	 *
+	 * The speaker widget is the output endpoint itself and carries the name "OUT":
+	 * a pin switch on "OUT" ("Spk0 OUT Switch") then really takes the amplifier out
+	 * of the path. Behind a separate OUTPUT widget it did not, because DAPM counts a
+	 * SPK widget as an endpoint of its own, and the speakers kept playing on the
+	 * headphone path, which feeds them.
 	 */
-	SND_SOC_DAPM_SPK("SPK PA", aw87339_event),
-	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUTPUT("OUT"),
+	SND_SOC_DAPM_SPK("OUT", aw87339_event),
 };
 
 static const struct snd_soc_dapm_route aw87339_dapm_routes[] = {
-	{ "SPK PA", NULL, "IN" },
-	{ "OUT", NULL, "SPK PA" },
+	{ "OUT", NULL, "IN" },
 };
 
 static const struct snd_soc_component_driver aw87339_component = {
